 17592186045417] [17592186153256 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153257 #edb/ref 1061 54190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153257 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a87b9ba-c67e-5da1-b438-76dadef85d15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153257 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that two variables, $x$ and $y$, are said to have a proportional relationship if their ratio is constant. The constant of proportionality $k$ is given by\n\n$$\nk = \\dfrac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the equation above as follows:\n\n$$\ny = kx\n$$\n\nThe following statements are all equivalent:\n\n- $y = kx$\n- $y$ **varies directly** with $x$\n- $y$ is **directly proportional** to $x$\n- $y \\propto x$\n\nProportional relationships frequently occur in real-world problems. Let's see an example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1065 8191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "cd20b689-18a3-54cb-97a9-7fa52d610ec1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153437 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
